<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n47744" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tĕnācĭtas</span></b> ,
			ātis, f.
		tenax, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a holding fast</i>, <i>tenacity</i> (very rare).
			* </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> In gen.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">(animalia) cibum partim unguium tenacitate
					arripiunt,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. N. D. 2, 47, 122</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Plin. 9, 29, 46, §
			86</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			In partic., <i>a holding fast to money</i>, <i>niggardliness</i>, <i>parsimony</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Liv.
				34, 7, 4</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
